          "verdict": "issue",
          "quote": "To make a negative stronger, use **at all**; **completely** after **not** means *not all of it*.",
          "severity": "blocking",
          "family": "learner-error",
          "reason": "The claim is too absolute. “Completely” before “not” can intensify the negative, while “not completely” normally means only partly."
